\begin{cases}
2x - y = 3 \\
x + y = 1
\end{cases}
\] Add the two equations together to eliminate \( y \): \[ (2x - y) + (x + y) = 3 + 1 \] \[ 3x = 4 \] \[ x = \frac{4}{3} \] Substitute \( x = \frac{4}{3} \) into the second equation to solve for \( y \): \[ \frac{4}{3} + y = 1 \] \[ y = 1 - \frac{4}{3} \] \[ y = \frac{3}{3} - \frac{4}{3} \] \[ y = -\frac{1}{3} \] Now, we need to compute \( 8x - 7y \): \[ 8x - 7y = 8 \left( \frac{4}{3} \right) - 7 \left( -\frac{1}{3} \right) \] \[ 8x - 7y = \frac{32}{3} + \frac{7}{3} \] \[ 8x - 7y = \frac{32 + 7}{3} \] \[ 8x - 7y = \frac{39}{3} \] \[ 8x - 7y = 13 \] So, the value of \( 8x - 7y \) is \( 13 \). </think> <answer> 13 </answer>

